  <ferc:NotesToFinancialStatementsTextBlock id="f103" contextRef="c1">&lt;div&gt;
&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 11pt;line-height: 107.9%;margin-bottom: 8pt;margin-top: 0;"&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 11pt;;display:inline;"&gt;&lt;div style="font-style:italic;display:inline;"&gt;&lt;div style="font-weight:bold;display:inline;"&gt;Financial statements&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 11pt;font-style: ;font-weight: ;;display:inline;"&gt;: The accompanying financial statements were prepared in accordance with the accounting requirements of the Federal Energy Regulatory Commission (FERC) as set forth in its applicable Uniform System of Accounts and published accounting releases, which constitutes a comprehensive basis of accounting other than principles generally accepted in the United States of America. &lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 11pt;line-height: 107.9%;margin-bottom: 8pt;margin-top: 0;"&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 11pt;font-style: ;font-weight: ;;display:inline;"&gt;The primary differences consist of the following:&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 11pt;line-height: 107.9%;margin-bottom: 8pt;margin-left: 0.24in;margin-top: 0;text-indent: -0.24in;"&gt;&lt;div style="color: black;font-family: &#39;symbol&#39;;font-size: 11pt;font-style: ;font-weight: ;;display:inline;"&gt;&amp;#61623;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="color: black;font-size: 11pt;font-style: ;font-weight: ;;display:inline;"&gt;&lt;div style="spacecount: 4;;display:inline;"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 11pt;font-style: ;font-weight: ;;display:inline;"&gt;As required by the FERC, the Company classifies certain items in its Form 1 Balance Sheet (primarily the classification of utility plant and nonutility property and retained earnings) in a manner different than that required by GAAP.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 11pt;line-height: 107.9%;margin-bottom: 8pt;margin-left: 0.24in;margin-top: 0;text-indent: -0.24in;"&gt;&lt;div style="color: black;font-family: &#39;symbol&#39;;font-size: 11pt;font-style: ;font-weight: ;;display:inline;"&gt;&amp;#61623;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="color: black;font-size: 11pt;font-style: ;font-weight: ;;display:inline;"&gt;&lt;div style="spacecount: 4;;display:inline;"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 11pt;font-style: ;font-weight: ;;display:inline;"&gt;As required by the FERC, the Company classifies certain items in its Form 1 Income Statement (primarily the classification of the components of maintenance expense, operating revenues, and operating expenses) in a manner different than that required by GAAP.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 11pt;line-height: 12.0pt;margin-bottom: 5pt;margin-left: 0.25in;margin-top: 0;text-indent: -0.27in;font-weight:normal;;-webkit-margin-before: 0em;-webkit-margin-after: 0em;"&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 11pt;font-style: ;;display:inline;"&gt;&lt;div style="font-weight:bold;display:inline;"&gt;(1)&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-size: 11pt;font-style: ;;display:inline;"&gt;&lt;div style="font-weight:bold;display:inline;"&gt;&lt;div style="spacecount: 0;;display:inline;"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 11pt;font-style: ;;display:inline;"&gt;&lt;div style="font-weight:bold;display:inline;"&gt;Company Overview&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 11pt;line-height: 12.0pt;margin-bottom: 5pt;margin-left: 0.50in;margin-top: 0;text-indent: -0.25in;;-webkit-margin-before: 0em;-webkit-margin-after: 0em;;font-weight: normal;"&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 11pt;;display:inline;"&gt;&lt;div style="font-style:italic;display:inline;"&gt;&lt;div style="font-weight:bold;display:inline;"&gt;(a)&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-size: 11pt;;display:inline;"&gt;&lt;div style="font-style:italic;display:inline;"&gt;&lt;div style="font-weight:bold;display:inline;"&gt;&lt;div style="spacecount: 4;;display:inline;"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 11pt;;display:inline;"&gt;&lt;div style="font-style:italic;display:inline;"&gt;&lt;div style="font-weight:bold;display:inline;"&gt;Description of Company and Business&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 11pt;line-height: 12.0pt;margin-bottom: 10pt;margin-left: 0.50in;margin-top: 0;"&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 11pt;font-style: ;font-weight: ;;display:inline;"&gt;Cube Hydro Carolinas LLC was formed in 2017 and is the single member owner of Cube Yadkin Transmission LLC (Yadkin Transmission, TransCo, or the Company), which operates the Yadkin Transmission Facilities in North Carolina.&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 11pt;line-height: 12.0pt;margin-bottom: 10pt;margin-left: 0.50in;margin-top: 0;"&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 11pt;font-style: ;font-weight: ;;display:inline;"&gt;Cube Hydro Carolinas LLC is also the single member owner of an associated company, Cube Yadkin Generation LLC (Yadkin Generation or GenCo), which operates four hydroelectric power plants (High Rock, Tuckertown, Narrows and Falls) located along the Yadkin River in North Carolina.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 11pt;line-height: 12.0pt;margin-bottom: 10pt;margin-left: 0.50in;margin-top: 0;"&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 11pt;font-style: ;font-weight: ;;display:inline;"&gt;On February 1, 2017, Cube Hydro Carolinas LLC acquired Yadkin Transmission Facilities and Yadkin Generation hydroelectric power plants from Alcoa Power Generating, Inc. (APGI). Cube Hydro Carolinas LLC assigned Yadkin Transmission Facilities assets and liabilities to the Company.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 11pt;line-height: 12.0pt;margin-bottom: 10pt;margin-left: 0.50in;margin-top: 0;"&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 11pt;font-style: ;font-weight: ;;display:inline;"&gt;Cube Hydro Carolinas LLC is a wholly-owned subsidiary of Helix North America I, LLC.&amp;#160;&amp;#160;Helix North America I, LLC is a wholly-owned subsidiary of Helix Partners, LLC (HP).&amp;#160;&amp;#160;Helix North America I, LLC was formed to act as a borrower in a long-term financing arrangement entered into in October&amp;#160;2018. In connection with that financing, Helix Partners, LLC assigned to Helix North America I, LLC, 100% of the membership interests in Cube Hydro Carolinas LLC and Helix North America I, LLC became the sole member of Cube Hydro Carolinas LLC.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 11pt;line-height: 106.7%;margin-bottom: 12pt;margin-left: 0.50in;margin-top: 0;text-align: justify;"&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 11pt;font-style: ;font-weight: ;;display:inline;"&gt;On October 7, 2019, pursuant to the Membership Interest Purchase Agreement (MIPA) dated June 25, 2019, Ontario Power Generation Inc. (OPG) purchased 100% of the membership interests in HP through its indirect wholly-owned subsidiary OPG Eagle Creek Holdings LLC (OPGECH). OPG is an Ontario, Canada based electricity generation company, whose principal business is the generation and sale of electricity in Ontario and is wholly-owned by the Province of Ontario. As of December 31, 2025, OPGECH is the sole member of HP.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 11pt;line-height: 12.0pt;margin-bottom: 10pt;margin-left: 0.50in;margin-top: 0;"&gt;&lt;div style="font-size: 11pt;font-style: ;font-weight: ;;display:inline;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 11pt;line-height: 12.0pt;margin-bottom: 5pt;margin-left: 0.25in;margin-top: 0;text-indent: -0.27in;font-weight:normal;;-webkit-margin-before: 0em;-webkit-margin-after: 0em;"&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 11pt;font-style: ;;display:inline;"&gt;&lt;div style="font-weight:bold;display:inline;"&gt;(2)&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-size: 11pt;font-style: ;;display:inline;"&gt;&lt;div style="font-weight:bold;display:inline;"&gt;&lt;div style="spacecount: 0;;display:inline;"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 11pt;font-style: ;;display:inline;"&gt;&lt;div style="font-weight:bold;display:inline;"&gt;Basis of Presentation and Summary of Significant Accounting Policies&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 11pt;line-height: 12.0pt;margin-bottom: 5pt;margin-left: 0.50in;margin-top: 0;text-indent: -0.25in;;-webkit-margin-before: 0em;-webkit-margin-after: 0em;;font-weight: normal;"&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 11pt;;display:inline;"&gt;&lt;div style="font-style:italic;display:inline;"&gt;&lt;div style="font-weight:bold;display:inline;"&gt;(a)&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-size: 11pt;;display:inline;"&gt;&lt;div style="font-style:italic;display:inline;"&gt;&lt;div style="font-weight:bold;display:inline;"&gt;&lt;div style="spacecount: 4;;display:inline;"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 11pt;;display:inline;"&gt;&lt;div style="font-style:italic;display:inline;"&gt;&lt;div style="font-weight:bold;display:inline;"&gt;Basis of Presentation&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 11pt;line-height: 12.0pt;margin-bottom: 10pt;margin-left: 0.50in;margin-top: 0;"&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 11pt;font-style: ;font-weight: ;;display:inline;"&gt;The accompanying financial statements have been prepared for the purpose of presenting the financial position of the Company as of December 31, 2025 and 2024; and the operating results of the Company for the year ended December 31, 2025 and December&amp;#160;31, 2024. &lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 11pt;line-height: 12.0pt;margin-bottom: 10pt;margin-left: 0.50in;margin-top: 0;"&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 11pt;font-style: ;font-weight: ;;display:inline;"&gt;The accompanying financial statements are prepared using the accounting practices prescribed or permitted by the Federal Energy Regulatory Commission (FERC), as set forth in the applicable Uniform System of Accounts (USoA) and published accounting releases. This basis of accounting reflects the accounting and ratemaking treatment authorized by the FERC, which is a comprehensive basis of accounting that differs from accounting principles generally accepted in the United States (GAAP).&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 11pt;line-height: 12.0pt;margin-bottom: 5pt;margin-left: 0.50in;margin-top: 0;text-indent: -0.25in;;-webkit-margin-before: 0em;-webkit-margin-after: 0em;;font-weight: normal;"&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 11pt;;display:inline;"&gt;&lt;div style="font-style:italic;display:inline;"&gt;&lt;div style="font-weight:bold;display:inline;"&gt;(b)&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-size: 11pt;;display:inline;"&gt;&lt;div style="font-style:italic;display:inline;"&gt;&lt;div style="font-weight:bold;display:inline;"&gt;&lt;div style="spacecount: 4;;display:inline;"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 11pt;;display:inline;"&gt;&lt;div style="font-style:italic;display:inline;"&gt;&lt;div style="font-weight:bold;display:inline;"&gt;Use of Estimates&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 11pt;line-height: 106.7%;margin-bottom: 12pt;margin-left: 0.50in;margin-top: 0;text-align: justify;"&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 11pt;font-style: ;font-weight: ;;display:inline;"&gt;The preparation of the consolidated financial statements in conformity with US GAAP requires management to make estimates and assumptions that affect the reported amounts of certain types of assets, liabilities, revenues, and expenses in consolidated financial statements and accompanying notes. Management evaluates these estimates on an ongoing basis based upon historical experience, current conditions and assumptions believed to be reasonable at the time the estimate is made, with any adjustments recognized in the period incurred. Significant estimates are included in the determination of contingencies and depreciation expense. Actual results could differ from those estimates.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 11pt;line-height: 12.0pt;margin-bottom: 5pt;margin-left: 0.50in;margin-top: 0;text-indent: -0.25in;;-webkit-margin-before: 0em;-webkit-margin-after: 0em;;font-weight: normal;"&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 11pt;;display:inline;"&gt;&lt;div style="font-style:italic;display:inline;"&gt;&lt;div style="font-weight:bold;display:inline;"&gt;(c)&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-size: 11pt;;display:inline;"&gt;&lt;div style="font-style:italic;display:inline;"&gt;&lt;div style="font-weight:bold;display:inline;"&gt;&lt;div style="spacecount: 4;;display:inline;"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 11pt;;display:inline;"&gt;&lt;div style="font-style:italic;display:inline;"&gt;&lt;div style="font-weight:bold;display:inline;"&gt;Cash and Cash Equivalents&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 11pt;line-height: 12.0pt;margin-bottom: 10pt;margin-left: 0.50in;margin-top: 0;"&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 11pt;font-style: ;font-weight: ;;display:inline;"&gt;The Company considers all highly liquid investments with original maturities of three&amp;#160;months or less to be cash equivalents that are stated at costs which approximate fair value.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 11pt;line-height: 12.0pt;margin-bottom: 5pt;margin-left: 0.50in;margin-top: 0;text-indent: -0.25in;;-webkit-margin-before: 0em;-webkit-margin-after: 0em;;font-weight: normal;"&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 11pt;;display:inline;"&gt;&lt;div style="font-style:italic;display:inline;"&gt;&lt;div style="font-weight:bold;display:inline;"&gt;(d)&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-size: 11pt;;display:inline;"&gt;&lt;div style="font-style:italic;display:inline;"&gt;&lt;div style="font-weight:bold;display:inline;"&gt;&lt;div style="spacecount: 4;;display:inline;"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 11pt;;display:inline;"&gt;&lt;div style="font-style:italic;display:inline;"&gt;&lt;div style="font-weight:bold;display:inline;"&gt;Accounts Receivable and Allowance for Doubtful Acccounts&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 11pt;line-height: 106.7%;margin-bottom: 12pt;margin-left: 0.50in;margin-top: 0;text-align: justify;"&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 11pt;font-style: ;font-weight: ;;display:inline;"&gt;Accounts receivable include both billed and unbilled amounts and are adjusted for the allowance for doubtful accounts and any write-offs. The Company establishes an allowance for doubtful accounts to adjust its receivable to amounts considered to be ultimately collectible, and charges to the allowance are recorded within general and administrative expenses or cost of operations, as appropriate, in the consolidated statements of operations. The Company&amp;#8217;s allowance for doubtful accounts is based on a variety of factors, including customer and industry credit conditions, collections, and historical payment performance. The Company&amp;#8217;s strategies regarding collection effort vary based on individual customer circumstances. There was no allowance for doubtful accounts established for accounts receivable during 2025 and 2024.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 11pt;line-height: 12.0pt;margin-bottom: 5pt;margin-left: 0.50in;margin-top: 0;text-indent: -0.25in;;-webkit-margin-before: 0em;-webkit-margin-after: 0em;;font-weight: normal;"&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 11pt;;display:inline;"&gt;&lt;div style="font-style:italic;display:inline;"&gt;&lt;div style="font-weight:bold;display:inline;"&gt;(e)&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-size: 11pt;;display:inline;"&gt;&lt;div style="font-style:italic;display:inline;"&gt;&lt;div style="font-weight:bold;display:inline;"&gt;&lt;div style="spacecount: 4;;display:inline;"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 11pt;;display:inline;"&gt;&lt;div style="font-style:italic;display:inline;"&gt;&lt;div style="font-weight:bold;display:inline;"&gt;Utility Plant Properties&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 11pt;line-height: 12.0pt;margin-bottom: 10pt;margin-left: 0.50in;margin-top: 0;"&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 11pt;font-style: ;font-weight: ;;display:inline;"&gt;Utility plant properties are recorded at historical cost. &lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 11pt;line-height: 12.0pt;margin-bottom: 10pt;margin-left: 0.50in;margin-top: 0;"&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 11pt;font-style: ;font-weight: ;;display:inline;"&gt;Depreciation is recorded using the straight-line method at rates based on the estimated useful lives of the composite assets: &lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 11pt;line-height: 12.0pt;margin-bottom: 0;margin-left: 0.50in;margin-top: 0;"&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 11pt;font-style: ;font-weight: ;;display:inline;"&gt;352 Structures and improvements (50 years)&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 11pt;line-height: 12.0pt;margin-bottom: 0;margin-left: 0.50in;margin-top: 0;"&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 11pt;font-style: ;font-weight: ;;display:inline;"&gt;353 Station equipment (25 years)&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 11pt;line-height: 12.0pt;margin-bottom: 0;margin-left: 0.50in;margin-top: 0;"&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 11pt;font-style: ;font-weight: ;;display:inline;"&gt;354 Towers and fixtures (20 years)&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 11pt;line-height: 12.0pt;margin-bottom: 10pt;margin-left: 0.50in;margin-top: 0;"&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 11pt;font-style: ;font-weight: ;;display:inline;"&gt;356 Overhead conductors and devices (25 years)&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-size: 11pt;font-style: ;font-weight: ;;display:inline;"&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 11pt;font-style: ;font-weight: ;;display:inline;"&gt;397 Communication equipment (5 years)&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 11pt;line-height: 12.0pt;margin-bottom: 10pt;margin-left: 0.50in;margin-top: 0;"&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 11pt;font-style: ;font-weight: ;;display:inline;"&gt;The difference between the historical cost and the cost to acquire Yadkin Transmission Facilities is recorded in Electric plant acquisition adjustments as noted in FERC Docket No. AC17-247-000 and depreciated over the estimated useful life that approximates the weighted average useful life of Utility plant properties. &lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 11pt;line-height: 12.0pt;margin-bottom: 10pt;margin-left: 0.50in;margin-top: 0;"&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 11pt;font-style: ;font-weight: ;;display:inline;"&gt;Repairs and maintenance are charged to expense as incurred.&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 11pt;line-height: 12.0pt;margin-bottom: 5pt;margin-left: 0.50in;margin-top: 0;text-indent: -0.25in;;-webkit-margin-before: 0em;-webkit-margin-after: 0em;;font-weight: normal;"&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 11pt;;display:inline;"&gt;&lt;div style="font-style:italic;display:inline;"&gt;&lt;div style="font-weight:bold;display:inline;"&gt;(f)&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-size: 11pt;;display:inline;"&gt;&lt;div style="font-style:italic;display:inline;"&gt;&lt;div style="font-weight:bold;display:inline;"&gt;&lt;div style="spacecount: 4;;display:inline;"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 11pt;;display:inline;"&gt;&lt;div style="font-style:italic;display:inline;"&gt;&lt;div style="font-weight:bold;display:inline;"&gt;Impairment of Long&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-size: 11pt;;display:inline;"&gt;&lt;div style="font-style:italic;display:inline;"&gt;&lt;div style="font-weight:bold;display:inline;"&gt;-&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 11pt;;display:inline;"&gt;&lt;div style="font-style:italic;display:inline;"&gt;&lt;div style="font-weight:bold;display:inline;"&gt;Lived Assets&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 11pt;line-height: 12.0pt;margin-bottom: 10pt;margin-left: 0.50in;margin-top: 0;"&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 11pt;font-style: ;font-weight: ;;display:inline;"&gt;Long&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-size: 11pt;font-style: ;font-weight: ;;display:inline;"&gt;-&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 11pt;font-style: ;font-weight: ;;display:inline;"&gt;lived assets are reviewed for impairment whenever events or changes in circumstances indicate that the carrying amount of an asset may not be recoverable. Recoverability of assets to be held and used is measured by a comparison of the carrying amount of an asset to future net cash flows (undiscounted and without interest charges) expected to be generated by the asset. If such assets are considered to be impaired, the impairment to be recognized is measured by the amount by which the carrying amount of the assets exceeds the fair value of the assets. &lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 11pt;line-height: 12.0pt;margin-bottom: 10pt;margin-left: 0.50in;margin-top: 0;"&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 11pt;font-style: ;font-weight: ;;display:inline;"&gt;There was no impairment loss recorded for the years ended December&amp;#160;31, 2025 and 2024.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 11pt;line-height: 12.0pt;margin-bottom: 5pt;margin-left: 0.50in;margin-top: 0;text-indent: -0.25in;;-webkit-margin-before: 0em;-webkit-margin-after: 0em;;font-weight: normal;"&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 11pt;;display:inline;"&gt;&lt;div style="font-style:italic;display:inline;"&gt;&lt;div style="font-weight:bold;display:inline;"&gt;(g)&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-size: 11pt;;display:inline;"&gt;&lt;div style="font-style:italic;display:inline;"&gt;&lt;div style="font-weight:bold;display:inline;"&gt;&lt;div style="spacecount: 4;;display:inline;"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 11pt;;display:inline;"&gt;&lt;div style="font-style:italic;display:inline;"&gt;&lt;div style="font-weight:bold;display:inline;"&gt;Income Taxes&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 11pt;line-height: 12.0pt;margin-bottom: 10pt;margin-left: 0.50in;margin-top: 0;"&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 11pt;font-style: ;font-weight: ;;display:inline;"&gt;The Company is a single member limited liability company for US income tax purposes. As such, federal and state income taxes are generally not recognized at the entity level but instead, income is taxed at the owner member level. Accordingly, for this entity, there is no tax liability, and therefore, no current income taxes or deferred income taxes are reflected in these consolidated financial statements.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 11pt;line-height: 12.0pt;margin-bottom: 5pt;margin-left: 0.50in;margin-top: 0;text-indent: -0.25in;;-webkit-margin-before: 0em;-webkit-margin-after: 0em;;font-weight: normal;"&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 11pt;;display:inline;"&gt;&lt;div style="font-style:italic;display:inline;"&gt;&lt;div style="font-weight:bold;display:inline;"&gt;(h)&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-size: 11pt;;display:inline;"&gt;&lt;div style="font-style:italic;display:inline;"&gt;&lt;div style="font-weight:bold;display:inline;"&gt;&lt;div style="spacecount: 4;;display:inline;"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 11pt;;display:inline;"&gt;&lt;div style="font-style:italic;display:inline;"&gt;&lt;div style="font-weight:bold;display:inline;"&gt;Revenue Recognition&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 11pt;line-height: 12.0pt;margin-bottom: 10pt;margin-left: 0.50in;margin-top: 0;"&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 11pt;font-style: ;font-weight: ;;display:inline;"&gt;The Company records revenue of transmission of electricity to others and miscellaneous services performed for others in the period that the power is moved or the services performed.&amp;#160;&amp;#160;Transmission charges are based on the Open Access Transmission Tarriff (OATT) schedules.&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 11pt;line-height: 12.0pt;margin-bottom: 10pt;margin-left: 0.50in;margin-top: 0;"&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 11pt;font-style: ;font-weight: ;;display:inline;"&gt;Unbilled revenue is accrued in the period incurred.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 11pt;line-height: 12.0pt;margin-bottom: 5pt;margin-left: 0.50in;margin-top: 0;text-indent: -0.25in;;-webkit-margin-before: 0em;-webkit-margin-after: 0em;;font-weight: normal;"&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 11pt;;display:inline;"&gt;&lt;div style="font-style:italic;display:inline;"&gt;&lt;div style="font-weight:bold;display:inline;"&gt;(i)&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-size: 11pt;;display:inline;"&gt;&lt;div style="font-style:italic;display:inline;"&gt;&lt;div style="font-weight:bold;display:inline;"&gt;&lt;div style="spacecount: 4;;display:inline;"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 11pt;;display:inline;"&gt;&lt;div style="font-style:italic;display:inline;"&gt;&lt;div style="font-weight:bold;display:inline;"&gt;Related Party Transactions&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 11pt;line-height: 12.0pt;margin-bottom: 10pt;margin-left: 0.50in;margin-top: 0;"&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 11pt;font-style: ;font-weight: ;;display:inline;"&gt;Cube Yadkin Transmission LLC (TransCo) transmits electricity generated by Cube Yadkin Generation LLC (GenCo) to the power grid and records revenue based on rates in the Open Access Transmission Tarriff (OATT).&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 11pt;line-height: 12.0pt;margin-bottom: 10pt;margin-left: 0.50in;margin-top: 0;"&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 11pt;font-style: ;font-weight: ;;display:inline;"&gt;TransCo and GenCo share some assets, employees, communications, resources and costs for operations and maintenance of TransCo:&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 11pt;line-height: 12.0pt;margin-bottom: 10pt;margin-left: 0.75in;margin-top: 0;text-indent: -0.25in;"&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 11pt;font-style: ;font-weight: ;;display:inline;"&gt;-&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-size: 11pt;font-style: ;font-weight: ;;display:inline;"&gt;&lt;div style="spacecount: 4;;display:inline;"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 11pt;font-style: ;font-weight: ;;display:inline;"&gt;The High Rock and Tuckertown substations are jointly owned. &lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 11pt;line-height: 12.0pt;margin-bottom: 10pt;margin-left: 0.75in;margin-top: 0;text-indent: -0.25in;"&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 11pt;font-style: ;font-weight: ;;display:inline;"&gt;-&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-size: 11pt;font-style: ;font-weight: ;;display:inline;"&gt;&lt;div style="spacecount: 4;;display:inline;"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 11pt;font-style: ;font-weight: ;;display:inline;"&gt;The Supervisory Control And Data Acquisition (SCADA) system is shared.&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 11pt;line-height: 12.0pt;margin-bottom: 10pt;margin-left: 0.75in;margin-top: 0;text-indent: -0.25in;"&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 11pt;font-style: ;font-weight: ;;display:inline;"&gt;-&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-size: 11pt;font-style: ;font-weight: ;;display:inline;"&gt;&lt;div style="spacecount: 4;;display:inline;"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 11pt;font-style: ;font-weight: ;;display:inline;"&gt;The employees are paid and managed by GenCo.&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 11pt;line-height: 12.0pt;margin-bottom: 10pt;margin-left: 0.75in;margin-top: 0;text-indent: -0.25in;"&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 11pt;font-style: ;font-weight: ;;display:inline;"&gt;-&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-size: 11pt;font-style: ;font-weight: ;;display:inline;"&gt;&lt;div style="spacecount: 4;;display:inline;"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 11pt;font-style: ;font-weight: ;;display:inline;"&gt;Shared assets are owned by GenCo.&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 11pt;line-height: 12.0pt;margin-bottom: 10pt;margin-left: 0.50in;margin-top: 0;"&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 11pt;font-style: ;font-weight: ;;display:inline;"&gt;GenCo allocates the cost of the shared assets, employees, communications, resources and costs for operations and maintenance of TransCo, and charges TransCo based on an estimated amount of time spent and resources used to maintain and operate TransCo.&amp;#160;&amp;#160;This estimate is reviewed and adjusted annually to ensure accuracy of actual time and resources spent.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 11pt;line-height: 12.0pt;margin-bottom: 5pt;margin-left: 0.25in;margin-top: 0;text-indent: -0.27in;font-weight:normal;;-webkit-margin-before: 0em;-webkit-margin-after: 0em;"&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 11pt;font-style: ;;display:inline;"&gt;&lt;div style="font-weight:bold;display:inline;"&gt;(3)&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-size: 11pt;font-style: ;;display:inline;"&gt;&lt;div style="font-weight:bold;display:inline;"&gt;&lt;div style="spacecount: 0;;display:inline;"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 11pt;font-style: ;;display:inline;"&gt;&lt;div style="font-weight:bold;display:inline;"&gt;Accounts Receivable&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 11pt;line-height: 12.0pt;margin-bottom: 10pt;margin-left: 0.25in;margin-top: 0;"&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 11pt;font-style: ;font-weight: ;;display:inline;"&gt;As of December 31, 2025 and 2024, the Company had zero in accounts receivable.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 11pt;line-height: 12.0pt;margin-bottom: 10pt;margin-left: 0.25in;margin-top: 0;"&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 11pt;font-style: ;font-weight: ;;display:inline;"&gt;There was zero of unbilled revenues as of December&amp;#160;31, 2025 and 2024.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 11pt;line-height: 12.0pt;margin-bottom: 10pt;margin-left: 0.25in;margin-top: 0;"&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 11pt;font-style: ;font-weight: ;;display:inline;"&gt;There was no allowance for doubtful accounts established as of December 31, 2025 and 2024. &lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 11pt;line-height: 12.0pt;margin-bottom: 10pt;margin-left: 0.25in;margin-top: 0;"&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 11pt;font-style: ;font-weight: ;;display:inline;"&gt;There was zero in accounts receivable - other, respectively, as of December&amp;#160;31, 2025 and 2024. &lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 11pt;line-height: 12.0pt;margin-bottom: 5pt;margin-left: 0.25in;margin-top: 0;text-indent: -0.27in;font-weight:normal;;-webkit-margin-before: 0em;-webkit-margin-after: 0em;"&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 11pt;font-style: ;;display:inline;"&gt;&lt;div style="font-weight:bold;display:inline;"&gt;(4)&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-size: 11pt;font-style: ;;display:inline;"&gt;&lt;div style="font-weight:bold;display:inline;"&gt;&lt;div style="spacecount: 0;;display:inline;"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;a style="text-decoration: none;"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 11pt;font-style: ;;display:inline;"&gt;&lt;div style="font-weight:bold;display:inline;"&gt;Accounts Receivable from Associated Companies&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 11pt;line-height: 12.0pt;margin-bottom: 10pt;margin-left: 0.25in;margin-top: 0;font-weight:normal;;-webkit-margin-before: 0em;-webkit-margin-after: 0em;"&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 11pt;font-style: ;font-weight: normal;;display:inline;"&gt;The Company also has $27.4 million and $23.1 million in accounts receivable with associated companies as of December 31, 2025 and 2024, respectively.&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 11pt;line-height: 12.0pt;margin-bottom: 5pt;margin-left: 0.25in;margin-top: 0;text-indent: -0.27in;font-weight:normal;;-webkit-margin-before: 0em;-webkit-margin-after: 0em;"&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 11pt;font-style: ;;display:inline;"&gt;&lt;div style="font-weight:bold;display:inline;"&gt;(5)&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-size: 11pt;font-style: ;;display:inline;"&gt;&lt;div style="font-weight:bold;display:inline;"&gt;&lt;div style="spacecount: 0;;display:inline;"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 11pt;font-style: ;;display:inline;"&gt;&lt;div style="font-weight:bold;display:inline;"&gt;Prepaid Expenses&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 11pt;line-height: 12.0pt;margin-bottom: 10pt;margin-left: 0.25in;margin-top: 0;"&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 11pt;font-style: ;font-weight: ;;display:inline;"&gt;Prepaid expenses consist of prepaid software subscriptions, totaling $115 thousand and $54 thousand at December&amp;#160;31, 2025 and 2024, respectively.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 11pt;line-height: 12.0pt;margin-bottom: 10pt;margin-left: 0.25in;margin-top: 0;"&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 11pt;font-style: ;font-weight: ;;display:inline;"&gt;Prepaid expenses represent payments made in advance that are recorded on the balance sheets at the time of payment and recorded as an expense to the statements of operations on a monthly basis over the life of the contract.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 11pt;line-height: 12.0pt;margin-bottom: 5pt;margin-left: 0.25in;margin-top: 0;text-indent: -0.27in;font-weight:normal;;-webkit-margin-before: 0em;-webkit-margin-after: 0em;"&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 11pt;font-style: ;;display:inline;"&gt;&lt;div style="font-weight:bold;display:inline;"&gt;(6)&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-size: 11pt;font-style: ;;display:inline;"&gt;&lt;div style="font-weight:bold;display:inline;"&gt;&lt;div style="spacecount: 0;;display:inline;"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#1